// Aetherium HUD kit (zone_source/aetherium_hud.zpkg — lua rawfiles, kit
// gsc/csc, images, fonts, localize; assets installed in the shared tools root)
include,aetherium_hud
// THE MAP TYPEFACE AS A TTF (2026-09-25): tools/build_tod_ttf.py builds it from the
// glyph sheets; the pause menu, its buttons and the scoreboard setTTF it. Zoned HERE,
// not in the zpkg, so the asset lint can see it.
ttf,fonts/tod_tower1.ttf
// v13.6 — ALXS CW/BO6 Pack-a-Punch (crown machine): models+anims+fx+scripts
// ride this zpkg (installed at share\zone_source\alxs_cwpap.zpkg); sounds via
// the szc ALIAS entry. Credits: Madgaz, Owen C137, RiDD_Alexis31 et al —
// CREDITS.md carries the full list before publish.
include,alxs_cwpap
// v13.9 KNUCKLE-CRACK POSTMORTEM (user: "never got the knuckles animation"):
// the ALXS script calls GetWeapon("zombie_knuckle_crack") — a WaW/BO1-era
// weapon name that T7'S MOD TOOLS DO NOT SHIP, and no pack on this machine
// declares it either (searched: raw weapons, all GDT scan roots, stock
// zones). A `weapon,` line for it was tried and REVERTED — the linker says
// "Unable to load weapon" because there is nothing to load; the pack's
// feature silently depends on some OTHER install's knuckle port (likely
// HarryBo21's perks, which ship one). USE_HAND_KNUCKLE is false in
// zm_cwpap.gsc until a real knuckle weapon is sourced — flip both back
// together when it lands.

// Logical's Powerups — timewarp + infinite ammo (vendored 2026-08-20:
// scripts in repo scripts/zm/logical/powerups, GDT in repo source_data,
// model/texture binaries installed in the tools root, wavs in
// sound_assets/_logical; credit Logical + NateSmithZombies before publish)
include,logical_powerups

// =============================================================================
// zm_tod2_cybercity.zone — asset manifest for the linker.
//   - custom scripts use `scriptparsetree`, NOT `rawfile`
//   - stock framework scripts referenced via #using need NO entries here
//   - brush FACE materials need NO lines (auto-pulled); only non-face assets
//     (sky xmodel, LUT, FX, script-referenced models) get listed
// =============================================================================

// THE CYBERCITY SKY (v17.71, 2026-09-05, docs/104) — self-authored, rendered
// by tools/gen_tod_sky.js into source_data/tod_skybox/_images/*.exr and wired
// by the four blocks in source_data/tod_skybox.gdt (image -> material -> xmodel
// on Treyarch's stock t6_skybox dome -> ssi). The SSI (tod_ssi_cybercity, a
// clone of Nastian's acc_ssi_miami_night with ONLY skyboxmodel changed) rides
// in via the worldspawn/volume_sun reference; only the sky XMODEL needs a
// line. NEVER add a material, line for a sky material — the standalone
// sky_latlong_hdr techset compile FAILS on this install (map 1, zone :793);
// it must ride in transitively through the xmodel.
// LOCKSTEP with SKYBOX_MODEL/SSI in tools/gen_tower_map.js — the ssi carries
// its own skyboxmodel key, so the pair must move together or they fight.
// History: Miami night (Nastian T9 pack) v1-v17.69; v14.37 tried silver_dark
// map-wide and v14.40 reverted it because the SPIRE is meant to be the dark
// place (its fog hides the sky at any density, so this line only ever decides
// how the TOWER looks).
// v17.78: Miami again for the A/B screenshot (user: "revert back to the miami view");
// the yellow turned out to be the SUN VOLUME height (docs/107, fixed v17.80).
// v17.81: the cybercity sky is BACK on a correctly lit base (user: "Looks good. Lets implement").
xmodel,skybox_tod_cybercity
material,luts_t7_default

// MAP-NAME VISION — NEUTRAL, AND THE FILE MUST EXIST (root cause of the
// 2026-08-26 "permanent zombie-blood orange tint" report). The engine sets
// every client's BASE vision by MAP NAME: visionset_mgr_shared.csc
// finalize_initialization() -> init_fog_vol_to_visionset_monitor(
// GetDvarString("mapname"), 0 ), and the manager restores that name per-client
// (incl. after every down/revive). This map never shipped
// vision/zm_tod2_cybercity.vision, so the engine resolved a MISSING vision and
// rendered its warm-orange fallback — a permanent, boot-time, Origins-style
// "zombie blood" wash that no script grep could ever find, because no script
// applies it. Map 1 hit the same mechanism (its 2026-06-24 "gray screen on
// revive" bug) and this is its rule ported: the map-name vision ships NEUTRAL
// (byte-content == stock default.vision; a tint here would be FORCE-RESTORED
// over any scripted grade on every revive). Source: vision/ in the repo,
// synced by tools/sync_to_modtools.ps1 (the "vision" mapping).
rawfile,vision/zm_tod2_cybercity.vision

// BSP (compiled from map_source/zm/zm_tod2_cybercity.map)
col_map,maps/zm/zm_tod2_cybercity.d3dbsp
gfx_map,maps/zm/zm_tod2_cybercity.d3dbsp

// Audio (sound/zoneconfig/zm_tod2_cybercity.szc)
sound,zm_tod2_cybercity

// Class guns (Skye CW ports, installed in the Mod Tools; assets carry no _zm
// suffix — base + _up PaP form, the t9 pattern; all three altWeapon-screened
// empty = boot-safe). Sound aliases: sound/aliases/tod_weapons.csv
// (gen: tools/gen_krig_sounds.js — krig cloned from ak47, ak74u/m60 verbatim).
weapon,t9_krig6
weapon,t9_krig6_up
// t9_mp5 + _up UNZONED 2026-09-20 (docs/153): the skirmisher ladder is the
// Hellbound Saug / M1927 / C.A.R. now, emitted as cc_* twins (include,tod_twins).
// t6_mk48 + _up UNZONED 2026-09-23 (docs/157): the heavy is the BREACHER now
// (Mozambique / 870 / Peacekeeper as cc_* twins); no script names the raw Mk 48
// and its alias rows are gone.
// t9_streetsweeper + _up UNZONED 2026-09-03 (docs/86 §8): the retired MEDIC
// class's gun — no register_gun, no twins block, no script reference since the
// class went; it cost 46 MB of pack and 30 alias rows for nothing. The Skye
// GDT stays installed; re-zoning is these two lines + the KEEP block in
// tools/gen_tod_sounds.js.
// SLASHER's melee = BOCW Baseball Bat (American variant), ported by pmr360;
// vendored 2026-08-20, REPLACING the ballistic knife (user order). _zm-suffixed
// asset ids — engine strips _zm, runtime names are bare (t9_me_baseballbat
// / t9_me_baseballbat_up). PaP suffix is _up (t9 convention, NOT _upgraded).
// Pure melee (no thrown component) — the ballistic-knife handler is gone.
weapon,t9_me_baseballbat_zm
weapon,t9_me_baseballbat_up_zm

// PER-CLASS SECONDARIES (user 2026-08-23). Each class gets its own sidearm
// instead of everyone sharing pistol_standard: SKIRMISHER the AW Bulldog,
// ASSAULT the CW Magnum, SLASHER the CW AMP63, HEAVY keeps pistol_standard
// (pure stock, needs no line). Base + PaP form only — explicitly NO twins
// (user: "They will all have PaP versions but thats about it"), so these are
// NOT in tod_twins.zpkg and gen_tod_twins.js never sees them. 6 registrations:
// ledger 159 -> 165 against the 200 guard.
// NAMES ARE AS INSTALLED, verified in the GDTs — note the AMP63's PaP asset is
// t9_amp63_rdw_up_zm, NOT t9_amp63_up. It resolves because the weapons CSV has
// an explicit upgrade_name column; do not "correct" it to _up.
//
// *** THE _zm RULE — this cost a boot on 2026-08-23, read it before adding a port ***
//   zone lines          = ASSET name    (KEEPS _zm)   -> weapon,t9_amp63_rdw_up_zm
//   weapons CSV + GSC   = RUNTIME name  (_zm STRIPPED) -> t9_amp63_rdw_up
// The engine strips _zm at load, so a CSV upgrade_name that keeps the suffix
// resolves to NOTHING. Stock resolves every upgrade_name while building the
// weapon table, so one bad name aborts init and dumps the player back to the
// frontend — the fastfile loads fine, the sound banks load fine, and there is
// NO script-error line and no crash dump, which makes it look like anything but
// a name typo. The in-repo precedent is the combat knife directly above:
// zone t9_me_baseballbat_zm  ->  CSV t9_me_baseballbat.
// Sound: all three are Skye ports, so their aliases are GENERATED into
// sound/aliases/tod_weapons.csv by tools/gen_tod_sounds.js — without that they
// link fine and fire SILENTLY.
weapon,t9_amp63
// THE AMP63's PaP IS A DUAL-WIELD PAIR — akimbo "Tokyo & Rose". The base
// (t9_amp63) is dualWield 0, but BOTH PaP halves are dualWield 1: rdw = the
// right hand and the weapon the CSV upgrades into, ldw = the left. Zoning only
// the rdw half is what aborted the map load twice on 2026-08-23:
//   Com_ERROR: could not find alt dualwield 't9_amp63_ldw_up_zm_zm'
// The engine APPENDS _zm to a DualWieldWeapon reference itself, so those two
// fields in skye_t9_amp63.gdt must hold the RUNTIME name — the same rule as the
// weapons CSV. They shipped carrying _zm, which is where the '_zm_zm' came from.
// INSTALL-SIDE EDIT (source_data/skye_t9_amp63.gdt, backed up as
// .tod-dualwield-orig): L10722 -> "t9_amp63_rdw_up", L11514 -> "t9_amp63_ldw_up".
// Safe to edit — map 1 never uses this GDT (zero hits in its zone/scripts) — but
// it lives OUTSIDE the repo, so a Mod Tools "verify" reverts it and the map stops
// loading again. Same class of install-side dependency as the HB21 ASM override.
weapon,t9_amp63_rdw_up_zm
weapon,t9_amp63_ldw_up_zm
weapon,t9_magnum
weapon,t9_magnum_up
weapon,s1_bulldog
weapon,s1_bulldog_up
// --- RIOT SHIELD (v16.63): the Lv5 "new model" form — Logical's standalone
//     Riot Shield weapon def (bulletweapon, weaponType riotshield, gunModel
//     logical_m_shield_full). Its GDT lives in the Logical pack under
//     <BO3>/model_export/_logical_models/ (gdtdb scans model_export GDTs), so the
//     weapon, line is the only inclusion lane. ONE ledger registration (guard
//     223 -> 224). The Lv1-4 shield is stock zod_riotshield: NO zone line — its
//     CSV row in zm_levelcommon_weapons.csv is the inclusion lane, and a
//     weapon,zod_riotshield line with no GDT on this box would hard-fail the link
//     ("Unable to load weapon", the cymbal-monkey lesson). ---
weapon,log_riotshield_zm

// Twin-swap variants (zone_source/tod_twins.zpkg, GENERATED by
// tools/gen_tod_twins.js): ak74u fire×handling(+ADS) combos + krig recoil
// ladder + combat knife swing-speed ladder
include,tod_twins

// THE WEAPON TABLE (review 2026-08-22, map 1 precedent — its zone line 1319):
// zm_tod2_cybercity.gsc::custom_add_weapons reads this CSV through TableLookup,
// which only sees a stringtable asset packed into a fastfile. Without this
// line the lookup silently hit the STOCK copy in zm_levelcommon.ff, so
// level.zombie_weapons never held a class-gun row, is_weapon_included() was
// false for every twin and the roof PaP machine refused every class gun ("PaP'd
// the PISTOL fine but never the class guns" — the cause _tod_powerups.gsc
// recorded without finding). The usermap copy (deployed by sync) overrides the
// stock table: stock rows + every generated variant row from gen_tod_twins.js.
stringtable,gamedata/weapons/zm/zm_levelcommon_weapons.csv

// Gift of Death (Xmas Gun XM53 wonder weapon by GentlemanCheeseMan; vendored
