// ---- THE GUN HUD (docs/91, v17.9). 59 images: the weapon panel and the
// offhand tile whole, plus 57 cells cut by tools/slice_hud_sheets.js from four
// delivered SHEETS — 12 weapon silhouettes, 3 offhand glyphs, and a custom
// typeface of 13 numerals and 28 letters/marks.
//
// The typeface names are built by CONCATENATION at runtime (TodGlyphImage in
// AetheriumLoadout.lua), so lint_tod_assets.js GATE A cannot see them from a
// Lua literal. That is the trap the 8 tier cards already fell into, so the
// lint parses this set explicitly — see TOD_HUD_GLYPHS there. Do not delete a
// line here on the grounds that "nothing names it": nothing names it in a way
// grep can see, and the failure mode is a silent WHITE SQUARE.
//
// i_tod_hud_lamp IS GONE, AND ITS CELL IS NOW THE MONEY SYMBOL (v19.2, user:
// "Our HUD uses this symbol in the player HUD when showing amount of money you
// have. You can reuse that"). The delivered ampersand read as an "8" and was
// never zoned or sliced; cell 28 carries the map's own points icon now, so "$"
// renders as that coin ANYWHERE our typeface is drawn. "&" still expands to
// " AND " in the name renderer — nothing drew it before and nothing does now.
image,i_tod_hud_lmoney
image,i_tod_hud_gun_gift
image,i_tod_hud_gun_katana
image,i_tod_hud_off_spider
image,i_tod_hud_off_spider_phd

